  "summary": "When invoked with `--remote-header-name` (`-J`), curl fails to preserve its",
  "details": "When invoked with `--remote-header-name` (`-J`), curl fails to preserve its\ndocumented anti-clobbering protection if an intermediate 103 Early Hints\nresponse precedes the final HTTP response, or if an `ETag` header is processed\nbefore `Content-Disposition` under `--etag-save`. This flaw allows an HTTP(S)\nserver to overwrite an existing local file specified in the\n`Content-Disposition` header despite the presence of the `-J` non-overwrite\nconstraint.",
